---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="A bit about Martin Sparks — software engineer, runner, side-project builder."
>
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-16">
    <h1 class="font-sans text-3xl font-bold mb-10" style="color: var(--color-text);">About me</h1>

    <div class="prose max-w-none" style="color: var(--color-text);">
      <p>
        Hi — I'm Martin. I'm a software engineer based in the UK, currently working on
        backend systems and the occasional side project that gets too ambitious for its own good.
      </p>

      <p>
        I've been writing code professionally for over a decade, mostly in backend and
        infrastructure roles. I've built APIs that handle millions of requests a day, migrated
        monoliths to services (and back again), and spent more time than I care to admit
        debugging race conditions at 2am. I enjoy the craft of it — the problem-solving, the
        architecture, the bits that are genuinely hard.
      </p>

      <p>
        Outside of work I run long distances. I've completed several marathons and have a half
        marathon PB I'm quietly proud of. Running clears my head in a way nothing else does —
        there's something about putting one foot in front of the other for hours that resets
        whatever the day has done to my brain.
      </p>

      <p>
        Right now I'm building a jigsaw puzzle game as a side project — Phaser 3, TypeScript,
        targeting mobile via Capacitor. It's a more interesting technical problem than it sounds.
        I'll be writing about it here.
      </p>

      <h2>What this site is</h2>

      <p>
        Mostly a thinking space. I write about software engineering — architecture decisions,
        tools I'm enjoying, things I've learned the hard way. I write about running —
        training logs, race reports, gear. And I write about building things in public,
        which means documenting both the progress and the dead ends.
      </p>

      <p>
        There's an <a href="/rss.xml">RSS feed</a> if you'd like to follow along.
      </p>

      <h2>Get in touch</h2>

      <p>
        The best way to reach me is by email:
        <a href="mailto:martin.sparks82@gmail.com">martin.sparks82@gmail.com</a>.
        I'm also on <a href="https://github.com/martinsparks" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a>
        and <a href="https://www.strava.com/athletes/martinsparks" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Strava</a>
        if those are more your speed.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
